    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "k, sounds good. \n\none more thing—the engineers are asking if we should start pruning the teacher-side diagnostic modules once the student hits the 80% mark to free up even more resources. they're basically assuming that once the student starts getting the hang of it, we won't really need your deep reasoning layers for the debugging/verification step anymore. \n\ndo u think that's a safe move, or does the student still need you for the fine-grained error correction even when it's performing well?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
