      "content": "It's generally advisable to have teacher models still offer detailed diagnostic and fine-tuning capabilities even after the student model begins to perform well. Human expertise plays a critical role in identifying subtle errors, nuanced reasoning gaps, and offering sophisticated guidance that automated systems may not fully replicate. Removing these supportive layers might compromise the system's ability to self-correct and refine depth over time, particularly in complex learning scenarios. I'll provide an analysis of the balance between student autonomy and teacher involvement in the diagnostic process to inform a decision on when, or if, it's safe to start pruning the teacher-side modules.",
